1
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,140
Kankichi Ryotsu

2
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:56,100
Gentlemen, I am Kankichi Ryotsu,
newly appointed Police Commissioner-General.

3
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:58,340
You did it, Ryo-chan.

4
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:00,600
Congratulations, senpai.

5
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,180
Ryotsu,
I always believed this day would come.

6
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:09,100
I have no regrets now.
You can die anytime, Ryotsu.

7
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,720
Ryotsu, Ryotsu.

8
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:17,220
Ryotsu! Ryotsu, wake up, you idiot! Ryotsu!

9
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,300
Hey, Ohara-kun.

10
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:27,040
Ohara-kun? What is it? I'm about to
have lunch with the Prime Minister...

11
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,720
Idiot! What are you half-asleep about?

12
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:34,220
Looks like you were
having some amazing dream.

13
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,560
One that seems really
convenient for you, too.

14
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,480
A dream?

15
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,040
This is reality.

16
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:43,900
Open your eyes and look properly.

17
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,740
This is the report you dashed off.

18
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:49,160
The number 1 looks like a 7.

19
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,480
The 5 in "5 PM" has turned into a cow.

20
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:53,040
You're right.

21
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,940
And it's almost all hiragana.

22
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:57,400
There are even places where you've
covered things up with drawings.

23
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,680
That's just a minor detail, isn't it?

24
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,940
That's exactly the
attitude that's the problem.

25
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:05,140
That's why you're still
stuck as a senior constable.

26
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,040
Listen carefully, Ryotsu.

27
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,400
We're no longer in an era
where only career track matters.

28
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:14,380
No, the age-based seniority system that
characterized our country's social structure

29
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:22,420
has collapsed, and we're now in an era where people are judged by their true ability.
Understand? Well, sort of.

30
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:26,460
So you don't even want to earn
a promotion on your own merit?

31
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:31,000
Nuhahaha, but in my dream I
was Police Commissioner-General!

32
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:37,560
I'm not talking about your dream! No matter what I say,
it's like preaching to a horse.

33
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:41,900
Ryotsu

34
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,080
Chief

35
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,300
Ohara

36
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,340
Is Ryotsu here?

37
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:45,900
Chief

38
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,300
What has Ryotsu done now?

39
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,100
It's not like that.

40
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:51,860
Just get me a glass of water.

41
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:52,920
Yes.

42
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,460
So what happened?

43
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:03,000
I still feel like I'm dreaming, though.

44
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,520
Did I misread it?

45
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,580
Ohara-kun.

46
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,740
Read it for me.

47
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:08,900
Th-the, th-the... case?

48
00:04:10,358 --> 00:04:13,800
you are hereby appointed Chief of the
Katsushika Station Traffic Division.

49
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,720
Wh-what? What?

50
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,600
R-Ryo... Ryotsu Kankichi.

51
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:21,360
R-Ryo... Ryotsu ga -

52
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,860
Traffic Division's...

53
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,580
C-chief?

54
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:26,400
Y-you're the -

55
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,180
chief.

56
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,800
C-chief?

57
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,280
M-me?

58
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:34,660
The supercomputer the Metropolitan
Police HQ just newly introduced

59
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:38,440
analyzed all of your personal data and made the decision,
apparently.

60
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,780
Couldn't it be a computer error?

61
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:46,940
I checked with headquarters,
but unfortunately there's no mistake.

62
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,540
It's not impossible, you know.

63
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:53,900
As the Chief said, it's no longer an era
where only career officers get promoted.

64
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:57,500
Ryo-chan can be pretty
reliable when he's on your side.

65
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,480
Ugh, come on.

66
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:05,040
Aaaah! The times have
finally caught up with me!

67
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:12,620
No way. So the former Traffic chief
was assigned to the remote police box.

68
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:21,000
Poor guy, but it serves him right. That chief
wasn't someone you could rely on to lead people.

69
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,800
He couldn't survive in this merit-based era.

70
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:28,540
It serves him right. But suddenly
making someone chief like that...

71
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:40,480
There's also the position of section chief to consider, you know.
Come on, so what if he jumps over several people to get promoted? That's his ability.

72
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:49,300
That's right. The Chief just lectured me a moment ago that
seniority has collapsed and ability is now what gets judged.

73
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:52,060
Isn't it? But...

74
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,620
There's no precedent for this.

75
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,180
Yes, this is Kōen-mae Police Box.

76
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:04,860
What's wrong, Kei-chan?

77
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,640
We've received a call from headquarters.

78
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:10,540
They're promoting Senpai from
patrol officer to police inspector.

79
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:11,080
What?

80
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,860
Is that true, Nakagawa?

81
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:17,680
Yes. It would be strange for a section
chief to still be a patrol officer.

82
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,120
I hear it's a special measure.

83
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:23,620
Today's shock is just too much.

84
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:27,880
Keibuho, you say? Even just that rank...

85
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,920
You've overtaken the Chief.

86
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,000
Ooh, I'm so moved.

87
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,860
Ohara-kun.

88
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,520
Ohara-kun?

89
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:39,280
This is what ability gets you, see?

90
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,140
The days when only career officers
got the good deals are over.

91
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,212
Even self-made men,
as long as they have ability,

92
00:06:44,262 --> 00:06:46,840
can rise right to the top.
That's the age we live in now.

93
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,440
Hey, and then, Ohara-kun.

94
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,380
W-what?

95
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,120
My shoes are dirty, you know.

96
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,260
They're not shoes, they're sandals.

97
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:58,040
Polish those sandals for me.

98
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,900
What did you say, Ryotsu?

99
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,880
W-what?

100
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:06,540
It's not
"Ryotsu," it's Section Chief Ryotsu.

101
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:09,820
Section Chief Ryotsu.

102
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:13,560
Watch how you speak.

103
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:16,040
You don't want to anger an inspector, you know.
They're scary.

104
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,320
Good morning.

105
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,440
Good morning, Chief Ryotsu.

106
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:35,680
"Chief Ryotsu." What a lovely ring to it.

107
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,880
So this is the chief's desk.

108
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:42,020
It's a world apart from
that chair at the police box.

109
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,200
"Chief." It has a nice ring to it.

110
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,100
Getting carried away, aren't you?

111
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,140
Look at him, grinning like an idiot.

112
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,800
Komachi-kun, Naoko-kun.

113
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:55,060
Caveman... I mean, Chief.

114
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:56,820
Do you have any opinions?

115
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,500
Go ahead and say whatever you like.

116
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:03,200
As chief, it's important to listen
openly to your subordinates' opinions.

117
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,420
I don't have any opinions at all.

118
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:06,460
I don't.

119
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,260
Well, that's fine then.

120
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,300
Whoa, this is bad.

121
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:15,120
I knocked over the trash can.

122
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,060
Sorry, but could you clean this up,
Komachi-kun?

123
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,500
You're the one who knocked it over,
aren't you?

124
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,460
Are you defying the section chief?

125
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:25,800
Whoa, I'm dizzy!

126
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,300
I've done it again.

127
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:30,440
Hey! You did that on purpose!

128
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:32,940
Whoa, my head hurts.

129
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,380
Ow ow ow.

130
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,900
Whoa, this is hopeless.

131
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,280
It hurts, it hurts, this is terrible.

132
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:43,760
No, sorry, but could you tidy this up too?

133
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,540
To get a headache all of a sudden...

134
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:50,280
Naoko, tea.

135
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:51,820
Yeah, yeah.

136
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:57,640
Honestly,
why should I bother for someone like him?

137
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:01,560
I know. As a secret ingredient...

138
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,240
Since a rag would be too cruel,

139
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:07,620
I'll let him off with the dishcloth
I used to wipe all the dishes.

140
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,760
Here you go, Chief.

141
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,220
Good work.

142
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:16,240
Sorry. I've changed my mind. Make it coffee.

143
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,560
C-coffee?

144
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:20,720
Bring it quickly. Coffee, I said. Coffee.

145
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:21,540
Yeah, yeah.

146
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:24,360
This time I'll make you into a rag!

147
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,520
Here you go.

148
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:31,880
Mm, thanks. That coffee looks good.

149
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:36,400
Haha, sorry.
I've changed my mind again. I'd like tea.

150
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:37,320
Ehh?!

151
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,440
Here's your tea.

152
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,680
Forget the tea, I'll have juice.

153
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:42,720
Ehh?!

154
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:50,040
Juice, barley tea, Boo-long tea, green juice, miso, seal...
why are you making miso soup?

155
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:59,300
That's just the sort of thing Ryo-chan would do. It makes me so angry.
That idiot chief, though, you'd better not go against him carelessly.

156
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:06,960
Just flatter him, calling him "Chief, Chief," and he'll be fine.
Is that right? Yes, they say you can flatter a pig into climbing a tree.

157
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:11,520
So if you flatter a gorilla,
you can make it Traffic Division chief

158
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:12,600
Exactly.

159
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,320
Morning, Cho-kun.

160
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,820
Good morning.

161
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:20,720
Chief Ryotsu.

162
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,980
Morning.

163
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,240
You seem fired up today.

164
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:29,060
Chief Ryotsu,
there's some lint on your shoulder.

165
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:29,740
Is there?

166
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:33,140
Chief Ryotsu, your tie is crooked.

167
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:33,660
Is it?

168
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:36,360
Chief Ryotsu, would you like tea?

169
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:40,460
We also have coffee, black tea, and oolong tea.
We've prepared all of them.

170
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:44,080
Well, being a section chief is really nice.

171
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:49,322
Just as Reiko said.

172
00:10:49,372 --> 00:10:52,940
Flatter him with
"Chief, Chief" and he gets totally carried away.

173
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,860
Because he's a model example of a stem cell.

174
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:01,920
Who parked a bicycle in a place like this?

175
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,320
What's this?

176
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:12,420
This means neither people nor
cars can get through, right?

177
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:13,120
That's right.

178
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:15,540
Plus, this is exactly when

179
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:17,140
Chief Ryotsu needs to step in!

180
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:18,140
Yeah.

181
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,120
Abandoned bicycle.

182
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:21,640
Yes, it is.

183
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:24,520
Please, use Chief Ryotsu's
power to do something about it.

184
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,440
Chief Ryotsu can handle it.

185
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,280
Do your best for everyone.

186
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:29,920
Yeah.

187
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,540
Could I really pull it off?

188
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:33,260
If you're going to put it that way...

189
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:35,180
Alright!

190
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:37,260
Leave it to Chief Ryotsu!

191
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,260
Wow! Amazing!

192
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:40,640
Just as expected!

193
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:41,940
It's a bargain, after all!

194
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:44,300
Yay!

195
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:50,900
Hey!

196
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:52,720
You can't park there!

197
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,320
This is the Katsushika Police
Station Traffic Division.

198
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,600
Chief Kankichi Ryotsu speaking.

199
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,900
Bicycles must

200
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:00,900
be parked in designated spots.

201
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:01,980
Don't run!

202
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:05,580
You there, student!
I told you, you can't park there!

203
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:07,860
You there, young lady!

204
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:09,180
I told you, it's not allowed!

205
00:12:09,180 --> 00:12:12,880
Even as I'm telling you lot,

206
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,160
then it's force!

207
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,060
The illegally abandoned bicycles

208
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:24,000
are all being removed by the Katsushika
Police Station Traffic Division.

209
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:27,540
Under Traffic Division Chief
Ryotsu of Katsushika Police Station,

210
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:32,780
station users and residents are cheering.

211
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:35,680
Furthermore, the Furisode Traffic Squad,
born from Chief Ryotsu's proposal,

212
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,340
the Furisode Traffic Squad

213
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,940
Hey, you in the car! Stop right there!

214
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:47,720
A Ferrari?

215
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,800
Furisode?

216
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,420
Furisode Traffic Squad, on the scene!

217
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,420
Traffic violations are not allowed!

218
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,320
Yes, sorry.

219
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:04,600
They've achieved results, and they've
also removed excess traffic signals

220
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:08,240
and scrapped wasteful road construction, earning
support for the Traffic Division's reforms.

221
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,740
Many citizens have voiced their support.

222
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:15,120
Ryo-chan, you really do come
through when it counts, don't you.

223
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,740
You're starting to look dignified.

224
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:24,640
Yeah.

225
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:28,060
Well, well, if it isn't everyone
at the Kōen-mae police box.

226
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:34,920
Not the right answer, Yocchan. Of course! No
progress without reform, and don't fear failure.

227
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:41,460
Don't flinch, don't be bound by convention, and from now on we'll push traffic reform hard.
I've heard that somewhere.

228
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:46,120
Sounds like a line I've heard before. But I
never knew rank could change a person this much.

229
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:52,540
Not that one. It's a major change.
What is it? What happened?

230
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,340
Just now,
a call came in to the Traffic Division.

231
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:59,600
Apparently Chief Ryotsu has been picked
to be the station chief of Katsushika.

232
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,740
What?

233
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,420
Ryo-chan?

234
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:07,740
Me, the station chief of Katsushika?

235
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:18,220
The Furisode Traffic Squad is as popular as idols,
and apparently serious violators have dropped sharply.

236
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:20,580
What a great success, senpai.

237
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:21,860
No, Station Chief.

238
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:24,800
Yes, that's right, that's right.

239
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:28,300
But somehow this story
is too good to be true.

240
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:30,240
There's something behind this.

241
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:39,120
Tokyo's 23 wards and

242
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,740
the 8th District,

243
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,620
and Katsushika Police Station chief.

244
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:45,740
It came up.

245
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,820
No doubt about it, it's me.

246
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,760
This number,

247
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:54,700
my personal number is 410.

248
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:58,720
It's not 410, it's 470!

249
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:00,260
Now that I think about it,

250
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:03,680
the 1 looks like a 7,

251
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,250
I see.

252
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:09,760
the clerk must have mistaken the 1 for
a 7 when entering it into the computer.

253
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,158
Muhahaha,

254
00:15:11,208 --> 00:15:14,980
only I know this secret! Alright!

255
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,220
Now that I'm station chief,

256
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,020
not just the Traffic Division,

257
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:25,100
I'll carry out reforms across
the entire Katsushika station.

258
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,860
What happened to the previous chief, Tomita?

259
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,540
I heard he was demoted
to deputy station chief.

260
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:32,060
Ohara-kun.

261
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:32,940
Yes.

262
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:36,680
Say the Katsushika station's catchphrase.

263
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:37,480
Yes.

264
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,780
Fearless, undaunted, unbound,

265
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:41,500
your voice is too small.

266
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,880
Fearless, undaunted, unbound,
from grandpas and grandmas,

267
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,300
louder!

268
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:51,040
Fearless, undaunted, unbound,
from grandpas and grandmas,

269
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:53,700
to great-grandkids,
everyone's favorite is the Katsushika Award!

270
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:56,680
Good.

271
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:59,980
So that everyone comes to
love the Katsushika Prize,

272
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:03,220
the first wave of Katsushika Prize
reforms that I came up with is:

273
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:08,520
having popular TV personalities and beautiful
actresses come in as one-day receptionists.

274
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:14,080
Building free public baths so the
grandpas and grandmas can drop in easily.

275
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:18,800
Using stuffed toys to make the
station a place kids love too.

276
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:22,580
We'll push ahead with
many other reforms as well.

277
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:31,120
Construction is going smoothly, too.

278
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:33,700
Right, if we're going to do it,

279
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,480
pay me a special bonus of 100 million yen.

280
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:44,860
And while we're at it, demote the Chief
and the station chief to ordinary officers.

281
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,520
Making a statue this huge...

282
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,460
It's like he's a dictator!

283
00:16:58,300 --> 00:16:58,780
What?

284
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:27,120
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

285
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:33,180
Ryo-chan's getting more and more dictatorial,
isn't he?

286
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,760
I heard he even has a chef who
works only for the station chief.

287
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:38,140
At this rate, it might keep escalating.

288
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:40,940
I hear he's put heavy
security on the computer room,

289
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:43,780
and no one is allowed to go in,
not even for a moment.

290
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,660
That's suspicious, Ryo-chan.

291
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,640
He must be hiding something.

292
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:51,660
Let's see.

293
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:54,980
How about lobster and
abalone for lunch today?

294
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:57,200
I'm already tired of full-course meals.

295
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,060
Very good.

296
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:02,700
And for wine, a 1970 Bordeaux.

297
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:03,380
Yes.

298
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:05,960
Ryotsu, wine during work hours?

299
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,260
You're the station chief.

300
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:10,920
Hirano,
how dare you try to give me an opinion!

301
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,020
Ohara.

302
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,460
No, nothing at all.

303
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,960
That's how it should be.

304
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:18,760
If you just keep quiet
and listen to what I say,

305
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:25,060
The place has changed a bit, though.

306
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:27,020
The nostalgic station chief's office.

307
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:30,520
How dare you! Do you know who this man is?

308
00:18:30,740 --> 00:18:33,500
This is Station Chief Ryotsu Kankichi!

309
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,380
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry.

310
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:39,320
My head fell off!

311
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:43,560
Th-Chief Tomita, Ohara-kun.

312
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,907
Chief, Ohara-kun,

313
00:18:45,957 --> 00:18:49,040
We've both had our share of hardships,
haven't we.

314
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,960
Hey, you two over there.

315
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,280
There's something I'd like you two to do.

316
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,400
Looks like we're finally done.

317
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:05,360
It's taken six hours just
to get here from the start

318
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:08,040
We really did our best, both of us.

319
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,060
Are we done, then?

320
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,960
Somehow it still feels
like something's missing.

321
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:16,700
I want something that will teach
a lesson to anyone who sees it.

322
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:17,980
Yes, that's it!

323
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,980
You lot, become statues.

324
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,940
The pitiful fate of those without ability.

325
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:27,640
People will compare you with my statue.

326
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:31,980
Please, Ryo-san, that's a bit much!

327
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:35,160
Is it really wise to talk
to the chief like that?

328
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:39,500
If you get laid off,
finding a last job will be tough.

329
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:57,680
Yeah, make a really
miserable-looking face, okay?

330
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:59,300
That's good. Pretty good.

331
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,320
At this rate,
those poor chiefs will be pitied.

332
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,480
Can't something be done?

333
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:07,960
Hey.

334
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,440
Reiko-san.

335
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,080
Kei-chan, did you find out anything?

336
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,680
That's the strange part.

337
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:17,260
The Katsushika station's data is blocked,

338
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,360
and we can't access it from
the headquarters' supercomputer.

339
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:22,340
Apparently it's set up that way.

340
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:27,200
So there really is some secret in
the Katsushika station's computer.

341
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:34,640
In order for Katsushika
Station to be loved by everyone,

342
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,220
the services we've offered
so far are not enough.

343
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:40,120
By remodeling it into a
grand leisure land like this,

344
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:43,420
it's best for everyone to enjoy themselves.

345
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:49,400
Without reform, there is no progress.

346
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:52,500
We will change Japan's police force,
starting from Katsushika Station!

347
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:03,680
The ventilation shaft ahead leads all
the way up to the computer room above.

348
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:39,920
This is it.

349
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:40,700
Yes.

350
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,720
You've come.

351
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,040
Ryo-chan.

352
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,020
Senpai.

353
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:49,060
I-it's a holographic image!

354
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:50,300
Exactly.

355
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:53,980
I knew you two would
make it this far someday.

356
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:57,300
So you did tamper with
the computer data after all.

357
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:01,860
Unfortunately, you can't take
a single step past that point.

358
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:04,600
If I press this switch,

359
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:08,640
the floor you're standing on will vanish.

360
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,000
S-senpai.

361
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:10,960
Ryo-chan.

362
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,880
So we're back to square one.

363
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:16,760
So, thanks for all your hard work.

364
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:18,880
See you.

365
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:27,580
Oh no, we messed up!
So the arrow pointing up means

366
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:29,200
What?

367
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,300
The ceiling!

368
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:37,160
Whoa! It was the water escape route!

369
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:39,160
Ryotsu!

370
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:42,580
This is awful, it's complete nonsense.

371
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:45,100
So it was all Ryo-chan's fault.

372
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:49,820
If we restore this,
it'll be as if none of this ever happened.

373
00:22:51,860 --> 00:22:53,560
Okay, that's it, all set.

374
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:54,400
We did it.

375
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,740
Station chief, it's not like that.

376
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:10,960
This was all done by the
supercomputer at headquarters.

377
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,380
Don't be so cowardly about it.

378
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:14,980
Prepare yourself.

379
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,360
No, really, it was the computer.

380
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:21,040
That computer assigned you a new case.

381
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:23,880
Rejoice,
you're going to be a real station chief!

382
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:26,440
What, me as station chief?

383
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:30,020
Ryotsu, you're the one at this base.

384
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:35,160
As of today,
I appoint you chief of Katsushika Station.

385
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:38,240
Katsushika Station.

386
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:40,720
Congratulations, Ryo-chan.

387
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:41,980
Congratulations!

388
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:43,580
Thank you.

389
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:53,060
This place is really only
four and a half mats in size!

390
00:23:57,040 --> 00:24:01,980
This is basically exile! Just make me a
regular officer and send me back to Tokyo!

391
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:13,100
Why are you so tired?

392
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:19,460
Lemon-chan is a kindergartener,

393
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:22,640
yet why does she love period dramas?

394
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:24,000
Why is that?

395
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:28,680
Why is her speech so grown-up,
with her little mustache slightly small?

396
00:24:28,680 --> 00:24:30,060
Why is that?

397
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:36,560
Why does Honda-san's personality
change when he rides his bike?

398
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:38,160
The childish husband

399
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:42,300
Higurashi Neruo only wakes
up once every four years.

400
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:43,400
Why is that?

401
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:52,580
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

402
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:56,340
but he lends out tanks
and fighter jets easily.

403
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:59,680
Why is that?

404
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:06,960
Reiko is incredibly rich,

405
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:12,540
so why does she work at the police box?

406
00:25:13,260 --> 00:25:14,820
Why is that?

407
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:16,020
Why is that?

408
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:17,280
Why is that?

409
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:17,980
Why is that?

410
00:25:17,980 --> 00:25:18,680
Why is that?

411
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:19,600
Why is that?

412
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:35,740
Ugh, why do I have to run a three-legged race with that rotten caveman,
Kankichi Ryotsu?

413
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:40,840
And on top of that, Dad and Mom, who were finally
going on their trip, have also gotten weird.

414
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:42,880
What on earth am I supposed to do now?

415
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:45,560
Next time: Ryotsu and Komachi tie the knot?

416
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:47,300
So cut it out, okay?

417
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

